{meta: title Better Times A-Coming}
{meta: x_lyrics_source bluegrass-lyrics}
{meta: x_lyrics_url https://www.bluegrasslyrics.com/song/better-times-a-coming/}
{meta: x_chords_source ultimate-guitar}
{meta: x_chords_url https://tabs.ultimate-guitar.com/tab/4053796}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Well the cows went dry the hens don’t lay
there’s no place I can [D]borrow
Give the landlord [C]all the news
and the [D]rent comes due [G]tomorrow
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Lots of money in the bank
they say that’s where they [D]keep it
Not only wouldn’t they [C]loan me some
they [D]wouldn’t let me see [G]it
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]So pick away on the old banjo
Keep that guitar [D]strumming
[G]Put more water [C]in the soup
There’s [D]better times [G]a-coming
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Well Mary Lou could pull a plow
if only I would [D]let her
Twice as strong as [C]any ox
and [D]she don’t smell much [G]better
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[G]I didn’t kiss that Mary Lou but once
and then I had to [D]leave her
Make’s my collar [C]get so tight
I [D]start to burn with [G]fever
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Well a man came by the other day
a-huntin manual labor
I told him I hadn’t seen the guy
why don’t he ask the neighbor
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
So come on boys get your gals
and kick your heels up higher
Don’t let no one steal your gal
just hold her a little tighter
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[G]My rooster used to chase a hen
he just kept getting [D]thinner
He nearly ran [C]himself to death
so I [D]bought him in for [G]dinner
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Cotton crops are mighty poor
the weeds are really [D]a-growin
I [G]need a woman [C]pretty bad
to [D]help me with the [G]hoein’
{end_of_verse}
